summary statistics are extremely useful  but they may not always tell the entire  story  in 1973 the statistician francis ascombe  devised the following data sets that  have nearly identical values for the  major summary statistics  but clearly the four data sets tell  different stories when graphed  more recently justin mateka and george  fitzmaurice published the datasaurus  dozen  all of these graphs have the same major  summary statistics as well  but each graph tells a unique story  the lesson is clear  don't trust summary statistics alone  you must always visualize the data to  see the larger picture
 

